<algorithms>
<!-- Arrows added from the original figure, 2026-11. -->
<algorithm id="fig001">
<meta>
<id>195.2</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title>Pediatric Obesity (Ages 2-18 Years): Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0564-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Plot body mass index (BMI) at all well child visits.</label>
<path target="cell-6">BMI &lt;85%</path>
<path target="cell-7">BMI 85%-99%</path>
<path target="cell-40">BMI &gt;99%</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Continue to plot BMI at all well child visits.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Prevention Plus Program for 3-6 months.</label>
<path target="cell-8"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-40">
<label>Prevention Plus Program for 3-6 months</label>
<path target="cell-24"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-8">
<label>Maintaining weight or decreasing BMI%?</label>
<path target="cell-9">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-10">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Continue Prevention Plus.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-10">
<label>Comorbidity or parental obesity (BMI &lt;94&#x0025;)?</label>
<path target="cell-9">No</path>
<path target="cell-11">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Advance to Structured Weight Management for 3-6 months.</label>
<path target="cell-12"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-12">
<label>2-5 years: maintaining weight or decreasing BMI &#x0025;; 6-11 years: weight loss or decreasing BMI &#x0025;; 12-18 years: weight loss?</label>
<path target="cell-13">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-17">No, 2-5 years</path>
<path target="cell-18">No, 6-18 years</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Continue Structured Weight Management.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-17">
<label>Comorbidity or parental obesity?</label>
<path target="cell-13">No</path>
<path target="cell-18">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-18">
<label>Advance to Comprehensive Multidisciplinary Intervention (3-6 months).</label>
<path target="cell-19"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-19">
<label>6-11 years: weight loss or decreasing BMI Percentage? 12-18 years: weight loss?</label>
<path target="cell-20">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-21">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-20">
<label>Continue Comprehensive Multidisciplinary Intervention.</label>
<path target="cell-23">If no improvement in 3-6 months</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-21">
<label>Comorbidity?</label>
<path target="cell-20">No</path>
<path target="cell-22">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-22">
<label>Age 6-11 years: BMI &gt;99%?</label>
<path target="cell-20">No</path>
<path target="cell-23">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-23">
<label>Advance to Tertiary Care Intervention.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-24">
<label>2-11 years: maintaining weight or decreasing BMI &#x0025;; 12-18 years: weight loss?</label>
<path target="cell-25">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-25">
<label>Continue Prevention Plus.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>The order of stages and time in each stage should be tailored to the child's physical&#x002F;emotional development and readiness to change. Adapted from Barlow SE, Expert Committee. Expert committee recommendations regarding the prevention, assessment, and treatment of child and adolescent overweight and obesity: summary report. <em>Pediatrics</em> 2007;<strong>120</strong>(Suppl 4):S164&#x2013;S192.<xref ref="pubmed18055651" resource="acc028" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
